cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Enforced Approval: Server-side approval of exact agent actions"
authors:
  - family-names: Iftikhar
    given-names: Sharoze
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6846-939X"
version: "0.1-draft"
date-released: 2026-11-20
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  This draft specification states the rules a server follows to refuse an AI agent's write unless an
  approval exists for that exact change. The server hashes the change, refuses it without a matching
  approval, and lets a person approve it on the server's own page or through a signed receipt, with
  single use, bounded grants and a hash-chained audit record. The release includes conformance tests,
  test vectors and a sandbox server.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - approval
  - authorization
  - MCP
  - Model Context Protocol
  - human in the loop
  - audit
  - specification
